---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/base';

const addOns = [
  ['Design Pack: 4 custom graphics or flyers', '$250/mo'],
  ['Social media management: 2 platforms, 12–16 posts', '$450/mo'],
  ['Extra social platform', '$250/mo'],
  ['Short-form video: 4 per month', '$450/mo'],
  ['Email newsletter: 1 per month', '$250/mo'],
  ['Google Ads management', '$450/mo + ad spend'],
  ['One-off flyer or graphic', '$150'],
  ['Event or seasonal campaign', '$600'],
  ['Extra change requests', '$125/hr'],
];
---
<Base title="Pricing" description="Weaver Digital's Get Found service is $99/month with no setup fee for the first 10 founding customers.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
      <h1>One simple <span class="light">price</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Everything in Get Found for one monthly price. No surprise bills.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="wrap price-layout">
      <div class="price-card">
        <span class="badge">Founding rate · first 10 customers</span>
        <h2>Get Found</h2>
        <p class="amount">$99<span>/month</span></p>
        <p class="setup">$0 setup fee</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>Website you can edit yourself</li>
          <li>Domain, hosting, security and backups</li>
          <li>Google Business Profile set up and managed</li>
          <li>Directory listings made consistent</li>
          <li>Review request link</li>
          <li>Monthly report</li>
          <li>One change request a month</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn btn-blue" href={url('/contact')}>Claim a founding spot</a>
      </div>
      <div class="price-notes">
        <h3>Your price never goes up</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          The founding rate is for my first 10 customers. After that, the price goes up for new
          customers, but if you start at $99, you stay at $99.
        </p>
        <h3>Six-month start, then month to month</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Plans start with a six-month term. Google takes time, and six months is enough to
          see real results. After that it's month to month with 30 days' notice.
        </p>
        <h3>My guarantees</h3>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><strong>30-day build guarantee.</strong> If you don't like your site, you get a full refund.</li>
          <li><strong>Six-month promise.</strong> If things haven't improved after six months, you can cancel with no penalty and keep your site.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted small">
          I won't promise you the #1 spot on Google. Nobody can honestly promise that. What I
          promise is the work, and a report every month so you can see what it's doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="add-ons">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Add-ons</span>
      <h2>Extras, whenever you want them</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Add-on</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {addOns.map(([name, price]) => (
              <tr><td>{name}</td><td class="price">{price}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <div style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <details>
          <summary>How long until I see results?</summary>
          <p>Usually about 90 days before you notice a real change, and around six months for steady momentum. If Google already lists your business but nobody has claimed it, fixing that can show results sooner.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Who owns my domain and website?</summary>
          <p>You do. Your domain is registered in your name from day one. If you ever leave, you keep the domain, a working copy of your site and your content, plus 30 days of hosting to move it.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I make changes myself?</summary>
          <p>Yes. You can update your hours, photos and services yourself anytime. For anything bigger, you get one change request a month that I'll do for you.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I pay?</summary>
          <p>Your card is billed automatically each month. No invoices to keep track of.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if I want to cancel early?</summary>
          <p>After the first six months you can cancel anytime with 30 days' notice. My 30-day build guarantee and six-month promise both still apply.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .price-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
    .price-card {
      background: var(--charcoal);
      color: var(--white);
      border-radius: 24px;
      padding: 36px;
    }
    .price-card .checks { margin: 24px 0 28px; }
    .price-card .checks li::before { border-color: var(--light-blue); }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--charcoal);
      background: var(--light-blue);
      padding: 5px 12px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .amount { font: 600 3.6rem/1 var(--heading); letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 8px 0; }
    .amount span { font-weight: 300; font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--light-blue); letter-spacing: 0; }
    .setup { color: #c9cad0; margin: 0; }
    .price-notes h3 { margin-top: 8px; }
    .price-notes h3 + p { margin-bottom: 28px; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .price-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
      .price-card { padding: 28px; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
